  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">North Macedonia: Strengthening the Criminal Justice Sector in the Republic of North Macedonia through Improved Legal Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To ensure that the targeted law faculties demonstrate commitment to sustainable criminal law legal clinics (CLLCs) operations. 2) To ensure that criminal law professors apply international standards of clinical legal education in CLLCs&#x2019; operations. 3) To ensure that national law faculties collaborate and share experiences on the operations of the CLLCs. 4) To ensure that national law faculties adopt best practices for teaching practice-based learning in applying the adversarial criminal law system. 5) To ensure that legal practitioners enhance the educational process of law students with skill-based learning. 6) To enhance students&#x2019; practical knowledge of the adversarial criminal law system.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Law faculties, criminal law legal clinics, law students and students&#x2019; associations. Indirect beneficiaries: Macedonian population.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to ensure that law school graduates implement best practices to adjudicate and prosecute criminal law cases under the adversarial law system.</narrative>
  </description>
